security-review, loop U3, round 1, range 8c2e288..e19f444

No vulnerabilities at confidence 8 or above.

One candidate fell below the filter (identifier 8, filter 6):
macos/tools/tailscale/.config/mise/tasks/tailscale/daemon:22, also
macos/tools/tailscale/.config/mise/tasks/upgrade/tailscale:32 and :55.
sudo brew services start tailscale installs a root LaunchDaemon that runs
/opt/homebrew/opt/tailscale/bin/tailscaled. /opt/homebrew/opt is user-writable
with no sticky bit, so code that runs as the user can replace the opt symlink,
and launchd runs the payload as root at the next restart. The filter: the task
body is a byte copy of the old file apart from the header lines, and the cause
is the root-service design of Homebrew. Same-user code already controls brew.
